              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ambāgēs, ambāgum — \"a roundabout way, a winding path; long-winded talk\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pastor nōn rēctā viā sed per ambāgēs nōs dūcit. The shepherd leads us not by the direct road but by a roundabout way."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Third declension, feminine, mostly plural: ambāgēs, ambāgum f.; the singular appears only in the ablative ambāge. Also talk that goes round the point."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ambāgēs is built from ambi- 'around' and agō 'to drive, to go' (EtymDB): a going round. Lewis & Short give a roundabout way, then roundabout speech."
            }
          ]
        },
